    "body": "## S005 \u2014 proof, counterexamples to auxiliary claims, and certified finite frontiers\n\n**Headline:** universal intended critical Almost Stacked Hypothesis (ASH*) remains OPEN for stacking and clearing. The printed-form counterexamples remain separately established. No premature phase-gate, novelty, Lean, Palomar, manuscript or author-contact claim.\n\n- Exact pure-pile clearing criterion is proved using an ancestry lower-bound argument and matching equal-level construction, explicitly crediting April Theorem 6.1 and October equation 4.10 for existing ingredients.\n- Acyclic balance scheduling sufficiency is proved, but a claimed acyclic necessity for clearing fails on K3 from 6e0. Distance-only two-site geodesic witness fails on a five-vertex triangle-tail, with replayable legal traces.\n- Global Q/lex extremal-selection remains an unproved strategy, despite all recorded finite complete cases agreeing with ASH*. Complete full-set independent recurrence replay, full reverse-winning bases, and symbolic/trace challenges are recorded in `sessions/S005/AUDIT.md`, `evidence/S005` and `research/S005_ASHSTAR_EXTREMA_AND_ROOTED_CLEARING.md`.\n- Reported campaign: 341 total cases, 340 eligible graph-goal cases, **337 certified exact thresholds**, 3 eligible cutoffs and 1 ineligible bipartite clearing sanity run. C10 stacking 63; triangle-tail5 clearing 190. No threshold claimed for any cutoff.\n- Reconciled session state, sources/claims, decisions, protocols, hashes, reproduction code and `authoritative/NEXT_SESSION_PROMPT.md` as **S006 FUTURE/UNEXECUTED**.\n\n## Publication integrity\n\nOne authored S005 commit **35efa0a818a5bc79f75b29ec8f36f8eb0149f089**, parent `9af432b717a1c742a9bed4708980ba7adf2da08d`, tree `6279be36cfa7b1fa5060ad72a0f2c74d3b27ef7a`. The owner pushed this exact immutable local commit to `session/S005-extrema-rooted-costs`; comparison to main is one commit ahead and zero behind (pre-merge). Check the actual **Governance integrity** hosted PR workflow, including the four S005 replay shards and the existing governance/S003/S004 validations, before merging; absent statuses/runs are not success. Preserve a standard two-parent GitHub merge (`merge`, no squash, rebase or force), then independently verify main SHA, tree and both parents and the post-merge main workflow.\n\nPost-commit/merge/check identifiers belong in this PR transaction record rather than inventing self-referential SHA content in committed research files.",
